<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15277" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ef-frēnus</span></b> , a, um (also
		effrenis mula, <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 44, 69, § 171</span></i>; Sen. de
		Ira, 3, 15, 2), adj.
		ex-frenum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>free from the bridle</i>, <i>unbridled</i> (not ante Aug., and mostly <b>poet.</b> for effrenatus; cf. also: infrenus, infrenatus).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 33, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>unbridled</i>, <i>unrestrained</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 382</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 465</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juventa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. Achill. 1, 277</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">profatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Silv. 5, 3, 103</span></i>
			.</div>
